1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,943
Chapter twelve — ingest what you already run.

2
00:00:04,003 --> 00:00:12,408
Most systems are not designed
from scratch. They already exist.

3
00:00:12,468 --> 00:00:19,905
Build has two ways in.

4
00:00:19,965 --> 00:00:28,112
Discover reconstructs the design
from what is actually running.

5
00:00:28,172 --> 00:00:37,616
It is the inverse of Deploy: it recovers
the services and their tuned dials.

6
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:46,622
Docker and Kubernetes come from the
local daemon and your current context.

7
00:00:46,682 --> 00:01:03,419
Azure comes back through the CLI — a
resource group, or a whole subscription.

8
00:01:03,479 --> 00:01:09,924
Import telemetry takes an OpenTelemetry trace.

9
00:01:09,984 --> 00:01:19,430
Spans become services, and the parent-child
links become the call graph between them.

10
00:01:19,490 --> 00:01:29,758
Discovery gives you the services.
Telemetry gives you how they actually talk.

11
00:01:29,818 --> 00:01:35,360
Put the two together and the design
on the canvas is your estate,

12
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:39,421
not an idealised drawing of it.
